sections.wikitext:
"Hot Stuff" was certified Platinum by the [[Recording Industry Association of America|RIAA]] and remained at number one on the [[Billboard Hot 100|''Billboard'' Hot 100]] chart for [[List of Billboard Hot 100 number-one singles of 1979|three non-consecutive weeks]], and spent the longest time in the top ten in 1979: fourteen weeks. The song also topped the US [[Dance Club Songs]] chart, with Summer's follow-up "[[Bad Girls (Donna Summer song)|Bad Girls]]" as a double A-side. "Hot Stuff" was the seventh biggest song of 1979 in the US.<ref name="USTop100"/> The popular 12" single edition of the song plays the full 6:47 version of the song and then segues into "Bad Girls" 4:55 version.

